      "description": "Pick the right case for each object pronoun: accusative for the direct object, dative for the receiver.",
      "sortorder": 1,
      "learningTitle": "Accusative vs dative pronouns",
      "learningPoints": [
        "The direct object of a verb is accusative (mich, dich, ihn, sie, es, uns, euch).",
        "The indirect object - the receiver - is dative (mir, dir, ihm, ihr, uns, euch, ihnen).",
        "Verbs like helfen and danken always take the dative.",
        "The form depends on the pronoun's job in the sentence, not on English word order."
      ],
